      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Praise is a direct constitutive half of 'praise and complaints'; captures the positive-evaluation aspect of the concept."
    },
    {
      "name": "complaint_terms",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Complaints are the other constitutive half of the concept; captures the negative-evaluation aspect."
    },
    {
      "name": "sentiment_polarity",
      "is_constitutive_facet": false,
      "role": "restatement",
      "rationale": "Overall polarity (positive/mixed/negative) restates the whole praise-vs-complaint balance rather than isolating a distinct aspect; it is a summary of the two facets, not a separate part."
    },
    {
      "name": "praise_terms.1",
      "is_constitutive_facet": false,
      "role": "restatement",
      "rationale": "Exact duplicate of praise_terms; adds no distinct facet and overlaps completely with the existing praise facet."
    },
    {
      "name": "complaint_terms.1",
      "is_constitutive_facet": false,
      "role": "restatement",
      "rationale": "Exact duplicate of complaint_terms; redundant with the existing complaint facet."
    },
    {
      "name": "sentiment_polarity.1",
      "is_constitutive_facet": false,
      "role": "restatement",
      "rationale": "Duplicate of sentiment_polarity; again a summary restatement, not a distinct facet."
    }
  ],
  "facet_columns": ["praise_terms", "complaint_terms"],
  "non_facet_columns": ["sentiment_polarity", "praise_terms.1", "complaint_terms.1", "sentiment_polarity.1"],
  "mutual_exclusivity": 0.25,
  "exhaustiveness": 0.55,
  "rationale": "Only two genuine facets exist (praise_terms, complaint_terms), which correctly carve the concept into its two constitutive halves. However the set is badly compromised: three columns (praise_terms.1, complaint_terms.1, sentiment_polarity.1) are exact duplicates and sentiment_polarity is a summary restatement of the praise/complaint balance rather than a separate aspect. The heavy duplication and overlap crush mutual exclusivity. On exhaustiveness, praise and complaint terms cover the two poles but omit finer constitutive sub-facets (e.g., which target of praise/complaint: acting, plot, direction, pacing), so coverage of the concept's internal structure is only moderate."
}

